# What the build context does not need, and what it must not carry.
#
# Two reasons, and the second is the one that matters now that this Dockerfile publishes
# a production image (sweep S25): a build context is copied into a layer, and a layer is
# world-readable to anyone who can pull the image. ".git" is the whole history including
# whatever was ever committed to it, and "data" is a live installation - its config.php,
# its database, its uploaded files.

.git
.gitattributes
.github
.vscode
.tx

# A real installation's data directory: configuration, database, uploaded files.
data/

# Composer and yarn output. Both are produced inside the build from the lock files, and
# copying a host's copy over them would replace a deterministic install with whatever
# that machine happened to have.
packages
public/packages
node_modules

# Coverage reports from a local suite run.
.devtools/coverage/*.xml
.devtools/coverage/html

# Local editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
*.tgz
